# Generated artifacts are compared byte-for-byte against their generator,
# so their bytes must not depend on who checks them out.
#
# core.autocrlf rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. The generators always write
# LF, so a clean clone ends up with CRLF on disk and the reproducibility
# check fails with a byte count no generator edit can explain. It passes on
# a workstation that happens to have already regenerated the file, which is
# worse: the failure only shows up on the machine that has none of the
# author's local state.
#
# -text means "take these bytes literally, never convert them". The generator
# is the source of truth, so the bytes it writes are the bytes we commit.
samples/card/anonymized/*            -text
design/prototype/common/card-import.js -text

# Note on the rest of the tree: this repository commits CRLF blobs. Do not
# add a blanket "text=auto" rule to normalise it. The blobs are not
# normalised today, so the first "git add --renormalize ." would rewrite
# every file and bury a real change under thousands of line-ending diffs.
# Migrating to LF is its own task, not a side effect of adding a test.